# WS-B degrade (a): a game with no .media cover is a plain {"name":...} item — still listed,
# no background. Two games so the index->file mapping is proven on a non-zero index
# (byte sort: "✓ Zelda.gba" < "✘ Alpha.gba", so Alpha is item index 1).
desc Game Manager: coverless games list plain; json index maps to the right on-disk file
config paired
seeded
sdfile Roms/Game Boy Advance (GBA)/✘ Alpha.gba
sdfile+ Roms/Game Boy Advance (GBA)/✓ Zelda.gba
pick 0|Game Manager
pick 0|Game Boy Advance (GBA)
pick 0|Alpha.gba
pick 2|
expect_exit 0
expect_trace LIST[Game Boy Advance (GBA)] rc=0 sel='Alpha.gba' fmt=json
# no cover fixtures -> no item may carry a background
expect_trace_absent LISTBG
# index 1 resolved to ✘ Alpha.gba (not the index-0 Zelda): action menu title is the raw name
expect_trace LIST[✘ Alpha.gba]
expect_trace_absent LIST[✓ Zelda.gba]
